; 17-local.kurt

; Not every `use`/`def`/proved theorem in a loaded file becomes available to
; you. Whether one does depends entirely on its label (10-load.kurt, 02-use.kurt,
; 12-def.kurt): a labelled fact is *exported*, an unlabelled one -- or one
; explicitly labelled `local` -- stays inside the file that wrote it.

; What crosses a `load`, and what stays (doc/kurt-ref.md, §8.2):
;
; | A `load` brings                                              | Stays in the file that wrote it                              |
; |--------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
; | its facts (`use`, `def`, theorems) with a label that is not  | a fact without a label, or labelled `local`                  |
; | `local`                                                      |                                                              |
; | the symbols those facts mention, with everything known about | a symbol that only local facts mention (and that the file    |
; | them: fixity, arity, `prop` places, sorts, `tex`, `lean`, ...| doesn't declare at its top level)                            |
; | the symbols the file declares at its top level without       | a declaration with `local` at its end (`const helper local`),|
; | `local` (`const`, `prop`, `infix`, `arity`, ...): its        | a declaration inside a block                                 |
; | vocabulary                                                   |                                                              |
; | the calculator bindings (`builtin`), `inline`, `tex`, `lean` | `var`, the constants Kurt added at a first use,              |
; | symbols; sorts and subsorts; chains; open `todo`s            | `calc on`, `default`                                         |
; |                                                              | a `def` written inside a block (it is local to the block)    |
;
; A fact that needs a symbol declared `local` can't be exported: the `load` fails, with the advice to
; drop the `local` or to mark the fact `local` too.

load local-helper

P                      ; fine -- "exported" was labelled, so it travelled here

; `Q` and `P implies Q` were never exported (one `local`, one unlabelled) --
; neither the symbol `Q` nor a fact about it arrived here, so `Q` can't be
; derived (the error even notes that `Q` was never declared):
expect "ProofError" "never declared"
    Q
; (`use Q` would not be an error: it just adds `Q` as a new axiom of this file.)

; a symbol itself is exported when an exported fact mentions it, or when the
; file declares it at its top level (`const pi`, `prop P`, `infix ++ 50 50`,
; ...: the file's vocabulary). `local` at the end of a declaration keeps it
; inside: local-helper.kurt says `prop Q local`, and nothing exported
; mentions `Q`, so `Q` didn't come along.

; `local` works the same way for `def` -- a defined symbol and the fact
; defining it travel together, or stay together:
load propositional
prop R
use R
def S iff R  local "s-hidden"    ; both `S` and its meaning stay right here

; this would fail if you tried it from a *different* file that only
; `load`s this one -- `S` was never exported, so it wouldn't exist there:
S iff R
